---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import Card from '@/components/Card.astro';
---
<Base title="Tools" description="Engineering tools for liquid cooling: a full-loop transient thermal simulator, a public CDU catalog, and three calculators for return-water grade, approach temperature and turnover readiness.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Tools" title="Engineering tools for the liquid loop" lede="Each tool does one thing a thermal engineer would otherwise do on the back of an envelope, and states the assumptions it makes. Use them to sharpen a question before you bring it to us or to anyone else." />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid c2">
        <Card href="https://sim.nextgenergy.ai/" num="01" title="Liquid cooling simulator" more="Open sim.nextgenergy.ai">Transient thermal model of the whole loop, from chip junction to heat rejection: pick a rack platform, climate and pipework, then watch junction temperature, flow, pressure drop and pPUE settle, and stress it with load steps, pump loss or fouling. Includes pipe sizing and a 3D view.</Card>
        <Card href="https://sim.nextgenergy.ai/catalog/" num="02" title="CDU catalog" more="Open">Public specifications for coolant distribution units from more than thirty vendors, each row linked to the vendor datasheet, with the rating conditions shown next to the capacity so the numbers can actually be compared.</Card>
      </div>
      <div class="grid c3" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <Card href="/tools/return-water" num="03" title="Return-water grade → feasible heat buyers" more="Open">Enter the temperature your loop returns at. See which off-takers can physically use the heat, which need a heat-pump lift, and roughly how much.</Card>
        <Card href="/tools/approach-temp" num="04" title="Approach temperature → CDU sizing" more="Open">See how the approach across the CDU heat exchanger moves facility supply temperature, and what that does to free-cooling hours in your climate.</Card>
        <Card href="/tools/leak-checklist" num="05" title="Turnover self-check" more="Open">Ten boundaries, three questions each. Score a project honestly and get a number you can compare next time.</Card>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
